{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — the flashnext:dev image exists (created 12 minutes ago, 18.2GB) — probably from a previous attempt's build... wait no, 12 minutes ago? The previous attempt was earlier, and maybe the campaign was re-run. Either way, the image exists and the layer cache is warm.\n\nThe previous attempt's container/ files are lost (not committed). container/ needs to be written from scratch. But wait — the image was built 12 minutes ago from a Containerfile that no longer exists. Layer cache: if I write a Containerfile with identical instructions, podman will reuse the cached layers, making the build fast. But I don't know the exact contents of the previous Containerfile. The cache matches on instruction text, so different text → rebuild. Hmm, but steering says \"re-running build.sh should be fast thanks to the layer cache.\" If the instructions differ even slightly, the cache is broken. There's risk. But a full rebuild takes 64 minutes.\n\nAlternative: maybe the previous attempt's files are still around somewhere — stash? git stash list? dangling blobs? Let me check git fsck dangling and reflog. The previous attempt didn't commit anything, but it might have stashed or left files somewhere else. I'll also check the podman build history — does `podman history` show the commands? Actually, podman inspect on the image shows the config but not the Dockerfile instructions. The intermediate layers (unnamed images) exist. `podman inspect` on intermediate images shows the CreatedBy commands, which might reveal the exact RUN strings, but not the full Containerfile text.\n\nLet me check git stash, dangling commits/blobs, and also other worktrees in the campaign directory — the previous attempt was probably on the same worktree path. I'll also check the build metadata in ~/.local/share/containers or podman.\n\nActually — the build was 12 minutes ago?? The image's CREATED is 12 minutes ago. The steering comment timestamp is 07:11 UTC. The current time is? Let me check the date. If the previous attempt built very recently and didn't commit the files... maybe the attempt is still running? No, this is a new stateless attempt.\n\nHmm, wait — maybe the previous attempt wrote container files somewhere else. Like directly into the repo directory instead of the worktree? The worktree path is specified in the brief. Let me search the filesystem for a Containerfile named flashnext.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_45e048ee36f04d489b39eb93","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"date; cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && git stash list; git fsck --dangling 2>/dev/null | head; git log --oneline tally-work/flashnext-a871de4d3faa/container-recipe -3"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_06bafda2a75d4f358b0fa68a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"find /home/tom/.local/state/tally /home/tom/.local/share/tally /tmp -name 'Containerfile*' -o -name 'build.sh' -path '*container*' 2>/dev/null | head; ls /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1955,"output":732,"cacheRead":18944,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":522,"totalTokens":21631,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787987980441,"responseId":"chatcmpl-063e541f-2f56-462d-a4b4-7899d242fce7","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_45e048ee36f04d489b39eb93","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sat Aug 29 09:19:59 AM CEST 2026\ndangling commit 5ee20022611be510f1105bbb59fc05cdd0192faa\ndangling blob cd201afb4b2126b9c8466d56a12a23e553f4d57e\ndangling commit d89f338f1e74622415022809f9becb28b73f86fa\ndangling blob f483a1b85f6931a5c4d901c61e2c52726386fc07\na428fee handoff: staging comple