Id":"chatcmpl-25ddcc37-72ac-4345-b819-5aab109527f5","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_44e79cb4038540619b62f745","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task container-recipe: Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"container\\\",\\\"results/receipts\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:9572f5f529de5e822547ebfc13b9ac97f3a9958ef36295fce8467a97479c1e64\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n container/build.sh && grep -q 'torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'mecattaf/vllm' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'flashnext:dev' container/build.sh && grep -qi 'MIT' container/Containerfile\"],\"description\":\"The recipe pins the exact wheel set, the fork branch, and the image tag, and is syntax-clean.\",\"id\":\"recipe-pins\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"A reproducible image build from the fork at the exactly pinned wheel set\",\"A build receipt the receipts gate can grade\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"THE PRIMARY ENGINE LANE of spec ruling P4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). Write container/Containerfile and container/build.sh implementing IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. Containerfile: Ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for GPU target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\\\"build\\\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. Credit the recipe shape to the MIT toolbox recipe named in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the Containerfile header. Boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.\",\"id\":\"container-recipe\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3\",\"IMPORTS.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:6e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361\",\"title\":\"Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"a428fee66b83d95682b418d5fdb4d975068e66ab\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-a871de4d3faa/container-recipe\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/container-recipe-6e8621b55de3a3a9\",\"taskId\":\"container-recipe\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER ADVISORY (arm-time): (1) A warm local wheel cache exists at /home/tom/.cache/flashnext-wheels/ on the coordinator with torch-2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, torchvision-0.28.0+rocm7.14.0, and triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0 cp312 linux_x86_64 wheels pre-downloaded from the vendor index. Your Containerfile must still reference https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (the acceptance grep requires it), but build.sh may bind-mount the cache dir and pass --find-links to pip so the multi-GB torch wheel is not re-downloaded at image build. (2) ubuntu:24.04 base image is already pulled locally via podman. (3) Do not add torchaudio — drop audio extras (the goal text is authoritative). (4) The build must ride ethernet (default route); never touch a 10.99.0.x address.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/2\"},{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER (post-failure insurance, applies to any future attempt): the previous attempt did all the work — authored container/, ran the full 64-minute build, wrote the receipt — then exited WITHOUT committing, and the driver failed it at ownership validation (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\"). Your final acts, in order, MUST be: (1) run the acceptance argv yourself and see it pass; (2) git add ONLY paths inside your conflict domains (container/, results/receipts/); (3) git commit with a descriptive message; (4) verify `git status --porcelain` is empty before you finish. Note the flashnext:dev image and its layers already exist in podman storage from the prior attempt — a re-run of build.sh should be fast via layer cache; do not prune or rebuild from scratch.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T07:11:19.614Z\",\"id\":4,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T07:11:19.614Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/4\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[2,4],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":4,\"recheckedCursor\":4,\"registrationId\":\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987946156},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me look into the worktree and check what's there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ac33aa46b7a54c07b1bfaaee","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && git status --porcelain && git log --oneline -5 && git branch --show-current"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b96b54f918094fa7b23cdc43","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && ls -la container/ 2>/dev/null; ls -la results/receipts/ 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2979,"output":176,"cacheRead":4224,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":13,"totalTokens":7379,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787987946160,"responseId":"chatcmpl-0c7c3643-425a-415c-b8ff-56f30921ff21","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ac33aa46b7a54c07b1bfaaee","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"a428fee handoff: staging complete, campaign launches attended-by-daylight not overnight\nf6db565 receipts: weights staged on both nodes (131 shards, 185563801379 bytes each)\nd62bd2f handoff: OVERSEER-LAUNCH refresh — routing read order, overseer owns the arm, weights pre-staging state, NCCL discipline\n0fbc61b README truth-up: pre-arm bake done, spec ratified, four host-bake findings, transport story, overnight compute routing\n14784f9 handoff: compute-routing doctrine (ROUTING.md) — tiers, per-task table, escalation ladder\ntally-work/flashnext-a871de4d3faa/container-recipe\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987951714},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b96b54f918094fa7b23cdc43","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 16\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 tom users 4096 Aug 29 09:18 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 tom users 4096 Aug 29 09:18 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tom users    0 Aug 29 09:18 .gitkeep\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tom users  139 Aug 29 09:18 weights-coordinator.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tom users  134 Aug 29 09:18 weights-worker.json\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987951714},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — the container/ directory doesn't exist in this worktree (only .gitkeep in results/receipts?). Wait, the first ls shows .gitkeep and the weights-*.json files — that was results/receipts. The container/ directory doesn't exist. git status is clean. So the previous attempt's work was lost (not committed). This time I need to write container/Containerfile, container/build.sh, container/rootfs/, and run the packaging tests, then podman build.\n\nBut wait — the steering says the image already exists in podman storage. But does the container/ authoring exist somewhere? The previous attempt didn't commit anything. Let me check the spec section first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_200a737d7f974b318ae9b614","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && ls && sed -n '1,120p' specs/flashnext/spec.md | head -200"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bb063da59cb6457db101583e","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && grep -n \"r3\\|3\\.1\" specs/flashnext/spec.md | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1441,"output":311,"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":145,"totalTokens":8024,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787987951717,"responseId":"chatcmpl-39abd3f8-dd1e-4e0c-911e-785bac4a2203","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_200a737d7f974b318ae9b614","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"docs\nflake.lock\nflake.nix\nhandoff\nhost\nIMPORTS.md\nLICENSE\npatches\nREADME.md\nresults\nscripts\nsilent-factory-worklists\nspecs\ntests\nTHIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\n# flashnext — the vendor FP8 release at tensor-parallel two on the coordinator/worker pair\n\nStatus: ratified 2026-08-28\nGoverns: silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\nConsumers: the flashnext worklist readFirst anchors; the S1 boundary sitting; the S3 morning review\nSupersedes: none\n\n## Outcome\n\nToday the pair serves nothing of this class: the stock engine refuses the FP8\nmixture layer on this GPU generation, the platform tree cannot load the FP8\nlookup table, and no container, units, or benchmarks exist for the pair. After\nthis campaign the estate carries a fork whose two patches admit the mixture\npath and port the disk-backed table onto the platform tree, a container built\nfrom that fork at an exactly pinned wheel set, host tooling that stands the\ntwo-node service on both rails with the wire as control, staged weights on both\nnodes, and a witnessed measurement record. Overnight checkpoints prove first\nlight on a proxy checkpoint, first light on the pair, warmed-decode residency,\na fidelity baseline, and counterbalanced benchmarks, each leaving a receipt the\nladder verifies. The morning operator arrives to a serving pair with numbers,\nor to a typed blocker naming its upstream cause with a drafted issue — never to\na silent skip.\n\n## Vocabulary\n\n- pair — the hosts coordinator and worker, two identical 128 GB unified-memory\n  desktops on the same fleet substrate.\n- rails — the interfaces thunderbolt0 and thunderbolt1, the inference plane,\n  socket transport only; one rail is cabled TB5 and one TB3, both trained at\n  40 Gb/s in the measured record, re-read at first light.\n- wire — the interface enp191s0, the control plane: ssh, orchestration,\n  staging.\n- workload checkpoint (NEW) — the vendor FP8 release at upstream revision\n  970c569adaca6b35532111fd6b27351b2baefe50; node-side artifact directory\n  /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8; full naming lives in README.md and the\n  evidence, never in this file or the worklist.\n- engram table — the 51.2-billion-parameter hash-lookup embedding inside the\n  workload checkpoint, read once per token at one layer.\n- fork (NEW) — the engine fork published as github mecattaf/vllm branch\n  flashnext; base commit 8e4e036a311604800334989485b4ee23925956da, the\n  table pull request's head, which already carries the model-support pull\n  request's model code.\n- admission patch (NEW) — the fork change that admits the block-FP8 mixture\n  scheme on this GPU and adds the in-kernel upcast, switch FN_FP8_MOE.\n- table port (NEW) — the fork change that wires the mmap table path and the\n  FP8 embedding stack into the platform tree the pair runs.\n- mmap path (NEW) — the disk-backed table mechanism behind VLLM_PLE_MMAP:\n  page-cache faults serve gathers, zero table bytes GPU-resident.\n- proxy checkpoint (NEW) — a small synthetic checkpoint with the same\n  architecture identifier and expert format, for single-node first light\n  before the real weights are touched.\n- engine build (NEW) — the fork made runnable per ruling P4: the container\n  lane tonight, the nix graduation lane once the patch set freezes; the build\n  receipt records which lane served.\n- container (NEW) — the image flashnext:dev built by container/build.sh from\n  the fork at stable vendor wheels, with a bind-mounted cached build\n  directory for incremental iteration.\n- pair service (NEW) — the orchestration under host/ standing both ranks:\n  container up on both nodes, distributed head and worker, then the serve\n  process at tensor-parallel two.\n- receipt (NEW) — one JSON record under results/receipts written by an\n  overnight step; the ladder gate validates every receipt against its bounds.\n- bench matrix (NEW) — the counterbalanced measurement protocol of ruling P12.\n- fidelity baseline (NEW) — reference losses and frontier logits captured at\n  first light, the yardstick for every later change.\n- morning ledger (NEW) — docs/MORNING.md, rendered overnight: receipts, open\n  items, promotion checklist, blocker entries.\n- RDMA package (NEW) — the operator-attended fast-path bring-up prepared under\n  host/rdma: pinned out-of-tree module fetch (never vendored), the single-rail\n  contract, the coordinated-reboot checklist, and the socket-versus-verbs\n  measurement protocol.\n\n## Rulings\n\n| id | decision | ruling |\n|---|---|---|\n| P1 | identity and timing | identity flashnext; the worklist and every gate id below are authored at this S1 sitting; the Governs line resolves before ratification |\n| P2 | workload naming | model-family names stay out of spec and worklist bytes (lint L16); the workload is named by revision and by the node-side artifact directory; full names live in README.md and evidence |\n| P3 | fork base | the table pull request's head is the base — it carries the model-support pull request's model code; the model-support branch's later head commit is CI-only and is not taken |\n| P4 | engine substrate | the container lane serves the night: stable-index torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 wheels — the fork's exact pin, published on the vendor stable channel — with the fork built from source in an image whose build directory is bind-mounted with compiler caching, so a one-line patch iteration recompiles only what changed; the nix derivation is the graduation lane, prepared tonight as wiring plus audit but never tonight's critical path — a moving patch set is not a thing to nixify, and the nix substrate charges a full recompile for every one-line change; the build receipt names the lane |\n| P5 | admission shape | the admission extends the upcast mechanism of upstream pull request 52970 to the fused-mixture oracle; refusal stays loud; FN_FP8_MOE=0 restores the stock refusal; no silent fallback is added |\n| P6 | cherry-picks | upstream pull requests 46012, 40963, 51511, 46110 enter the fork with Cherry-picked-from trailers; 44331, 46186, 46676 receive no task in this campaign and are recorded in IMPORTS.md for the four-bit lane |\n| P7 | transport | socket transport on both rails is the overnight transport of record, both rails named to the collective library; the RDMA package is prepared overnight but brought up only operator-attended, on one rail only, and only after a committed socket-transport benchmark is banked — the kernel half is entirely unpaid on this fleet, the worker's deploy path must move off the fast rail before any kernel change, the reboot order is worker first and never both at once, and adoption comes only on a counterbalanced win |\n| P8 | weights | staged library-to-node by scripts/stage-weights.sh with a per-file digest manifest; the fleet catalog row is a morning operator act prepared under handoff/; runtime hub downloads stay forbidden |\n| P9 | unattended overnight | GPU checkpoints run unattended; a wedge needing physical presence ends the campaign with the blocker typed in the morning ledger; no overnight reboot of either node |\n| P10 | first light mode | the table path's own guard demands piecewise capture with the mmap operation as a split boundary and refuses plain eager — first light runs that sanctioned mode; full-graph capture is morning work |\n| P11 | residency verdict | read after 50 warmed decode tokens on both ranks, never at load; GTT, RSS, and table page-cache residency recorded; pass bound 80 GiB per rank with zero table bytes GPU-resident |\n| P12 | bench protocol | three loads per arm, interleaved arms, medians, token fingerprints; depth series 0, 10240, 102400; speculative on and off arms; rows committed under results/ |\n| P13 | promotion | a morning human act; nothing overnight changes any fleet roster or default |\n| P14 | oracle provenance | the gate ids below are created in the governing worklist at this sitting; heavy overnight proofs bind through receipts validated by the receipts gate, and the trace joins each claim to its producing checkpoint |\n| P15 | compute routing | campaign adapter pi with the model unset — the host catalog answers; the fork engineering is estate bootstrap authored before arming and reviewed in-session |\n| P16 | blocker protocol | an unresolvable upstream defect ends as drafted issue text under handoff/upstream-issues plus a morning-ledger entry, never as a silent skip |\n\n## Claims\n\n### R1 — provenance and the public face\nWhy: every downstream judgment leans on the evidence corpus, and the repository is public from birth; a dangling citation is a fabricated fact.\n1.1 the seven sweep dossiers land under `specs/flashnext/evidence/` → the tests suite counts at least 7 (given) dossiers. [gate: repo-tests]\n1.2 `IMPORTS.md` names every external artifact with source, revision or pull-request id, license, and role → the notices file covers the same set, asserted by the tests suite. [gate: repo-tests]\n1.3 `README.md` states the project, the topology, and the evidence trail → the tests suite's secret scan passes on the published tree. [gate: repo-tests]\n\n### R2 — the fork\nWhy: the fork is the only path this class of workload can take on this GPU; its content must be provable from the estate, not narrated.\n2.1 BELIEVE:IMPORTS.md — the fork base is the table pull request's head commit 8e4e036a311604800334989485b4ee23925956da → the fork-verify gate confirms base ancestry on the published fork branch. [gate: fork-verify]\n2.2 the admission patch lands on the fork → the verify script finds the FN_FP8_MOE switch and the upcast plumbing in the fused-mixture layer tree. [gate: fork-verify]\n2.3 the table port lands on the fork → the verify script finds the mmap import, the FP8 dequant, and the relocated mmap module in the platform tree. [gate: fork-verify]\n2.4 the four ruling P6 cherry-picks land on the fork → the verify script finds each signature. [gate: fork-verify]\n2.5 every fork commit past the base is mirrored under `patches/` → the verify script counts mirrored patches equal to fork commits. [gate: fork-verify]\n\n### R3 — the container\nWhy: the pinned wheel set and the fork meet for the first time inside the image; the smoke step answers the cheap questions before any weight byte moves.\n3.1 the engine build lands through the ruling P4 container lane → a build receipt records status pass with the lane, the resolved torch and triton versions, and the wall-clock. [gate: receipts-verify]\n3.2 `scripts/run-smoke.sh` runs against the image → a smoke receipt records the GPU architecture string, a finite fp8 storage cast, the registered architecture identifier, the aperture, and the admission verdict. [gate: receipts-verify]\n\n### R4 — engine proof\nWhy: nobody anywhere has run this workload on this GPU at tensor-parallel two; each step below converts one unknown into a receipt.\n4.1 the proxy checkpoint serves on one node with the mmap path engaged → a proxy receipt records finite output and a clean shutdown. [gate: receipts-verify]\n4.2 the pair service reaches first light eager over both rails → a tp2 receipt records a greedy 300 (given)-token completion byte-identical across two (given) runs and the per-rail link speeds. [gate: receipts-verify]\n4.3 residency is read per ruling P11 → a residency receipt lands inside the per-rank bound with zero engram table bytes GPU-resident. [gate: receipts-verify]\n4.4 the fidelity baseline lands → reference losses and frontier logits are stored under `results/` beside their receipt. [gate: receipts-verify]\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987958556},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bb063da59cb6457db101583e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"112:3.1 the engine build lands through the ruling P4 container lane → a build receipt records status pass with the lane, the resolved torch and triton versions, and the wall-clock. [gate: receipts-verify]\n153:UNKNOWN-4 the fork's runtime behavior on the ruling P4 wheel set — drained by claims 3.1 and 4.1.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987958557},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"According to the steering, the previous attempt created container/ and ran the build, but it wasn't committed and was lost. In reality, the container/ directory doesn't exist in the worktree. Let me check sections 1 and 2 of IMPORTS.md, the toolbox name in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, scripts/run-smoke.sh, the packaging tests (tests/), and confirm the existence of the podman image.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d971ce59e3f542d7954be252","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && sed -n '1,140p' IMPORTS.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dfa95e2f30c54781ae9ee1b3","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && cat THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md; echo ----; ls tests scripts; echo ----; cat scripts/run-smoke.sh"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":3778,"output":244,"cacheRead":7168,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":88,"totalTokens":11190,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787987958561,"responseId":"chatcmpl-db6b25f1-e794-43ad-899f-d2b26f68c73f","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d971ce59e3f542d7954be252","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# IMPORTS — every external artifact, pinned\n\n*The authoritative manifest of what this repo consumes, from where, at which\nrevision, under which license, and why. Every row was verified against source\non 2026-08-28 (evidence: `specs/flashnext/evidence/`). Anything not listed\nhere is original work under this repo's Apache-2.0 LICENSE.*\n\n## 1. torch / wheel substrate — the versioning decision\n\n| Component | Pin | Source | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| torch | `2.13.0+rocm7.14.0` (cp312/cp313 per image python) — **container lane only** | `https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/` (AMD **stable** index) | AMD's stable multi-arch index carries this wheel for gfx1151 (verified 2026-08-28 — the index tops out at torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0). No nightly needed. Note the fork's `pyproject.toml` `[build-system]` pin is now `torch == 2.11.0` (Gate 0: the **nix** lane's TheRock substrate ships only 2.11.0, and the overlay's `--replace-fail` matches that literal; see `patches/0001-*`). This does not constrain the container lane: vLLM builds `--no-build-isolation` (and `[tool.uv] no-build-isolation-package = [\"torch\"]`), so `build-system.requires` is never resolved — the container's torch is whatever the image installs, i.e. this row. `requirements/build/cuda.txt` stays at 2.13.0. |\n| torchvision | `0.28.0+rocm7.14.0` | same index | torch 2.13-aligned. |\n| torchaudio | **omitted** | — | Only needed for vLLM audio extras; it is what capped kyuz0's auto-resolved set at torch 2.11.0. We drop the extra instead of downgrading torch. |\n| triton | wheel accompanying the torch set on the same index; fallback: the `pytorch-triton-rocm` wheel torch 2.13.0 declares | same index | Must be < 3.8.0 awareness: the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on `triton < 3.8` (see PR #52970 pattern below). Record the resolved version in the build receipt. |\n| ROCm userspace | rides inside the torch wheel set (`_rocm_sdk_core`, rocm 7.14.0) | same index | Stable, matches kernel 7.1.4 driver on both nodes. **ROCm 10 is out of scope**: AMD publishes no ROCm 10 gfx1151 torch wheels (`stable.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/` → 404; verified), and the ROCm 10 rocBLAS bump (5.5.0.cd957402 → 5.6.0.8d1ae90e) invalidates tuned GEMM solution indices. |\n\n## 2. The vLLM fork — `mecattaf/vllm` branch `flashnext`\n\n**Base: `8e4e036a311604800334989485b4ee23925956da`** — the head of upstream PR\n[#54129](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54129) (`Trosfy:ple-mmap-upstream`),\nwhich already carries the complete model support of PR\n[#53896](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/53896) (`peakcrosser7:release/qwen38next`)\nplus a fresh upstream-main merge. #53896's later head commit is CI-only and is\nnot taken. Verified: the two branches' model trees are byte-identical except\nupstream drift in 6 files where #54129 is newer, and `nvidia/ple_mmap.py` which\nonly #54129 has. (Apache-2.0 throughout.)\n\n### 2.1 Cherry-picks from open upstream PRs (committed with `Cherry-picked-from:` trailers)\n\n| PR | Title | Size | Why we need it |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [#46012](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/46012) | Fix Wave32 LDS overflow in top-k merge launch | 5 lines | **Load-bearing.** `top_k_per_row_decode` — the exact custom op the `amd/` QSA indexer calls — launches its merge at 1024 threads, exceeding the 64 KB LDS on wave32. 512 on ROCm. |\n| [#40963](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/40963) | Detect AMD APU, fix VRAM reporting for unified memory | 87 lines | **Load-bearing.** On this APU, hipMemGetInfo reports the small VRAM aperture as total; vLLM's KV-cache sizing then miscomputes. Reads sysfs GTT totals instead (8 GiB reserve). |\n| [#51511](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51511) | Disable skinny GEMM on gfx1151 | 96 lines | wvSplitK is \"pathologically slow\" on gfx1151 per the PR; falls back to torch GEMM. |\n| [#46110](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/46110) | ROCm detection via KFD topology when amdsmi fails | 170 lines | Robustness: platform + `_GCN_ARCH` detection without HIP init, straight from `/sys/class/kfd`. |\n\n### 2.2 Pattern adoption (not a cherry-pick)\n\n| PR | What we take |\n|---|---|\n| [#52970](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/52970) (amd-xavierwang, \"aiter Triton kernels + dsv4 on RDNA3\") | The **`FORCE_FP8_DOT_UPCAST` mechanism**: in the block-scaled w8a8 Triton GEMM, load fp8 A/B tiles then `.to(tl.bfloat16)` before `tl.dot`, gated `on_gfx1151() and triton < 3.8`. This is AMD's own sanctioned answer to \"no FP8 unit on RDNA3.5\". Our fork applies the same transform to the **fused-MoE** Triton kernel and admits `(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym)` for gfx1151 in `TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme`, behind `FN_FP8_MOE` (default on; `=0` restores the stock loud refusal). The aiter-library parts of #52970 are NOT taken (aiter excluded from the container this campaign). |\n| [#44331](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/44331) (tuned MoE configs for Radeon 8060S) | Deferred to the 4-bit lane (its configs are `int4_w4a16`, E=256). What we take now is the *mechanism knowledge*: fused-MoE reads per-device tuned-config JSONs — generating `E=512,N=640,device_name=Radeon_8060S_Graphics,dtype=fp8_w8a8` is a named optimization task once first light lands. |\n| [#46186](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/46186), [#46676](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/46676) | The future 4-bit expert lane (W4A16 GEMM on gfx1151; native HIP MXFP4 for RDNA3). Not in this campaign's scope; recorded so nobody re-finds them. |\n\n### 2.3 Our two original patches (the world-first pieces)\n\n*(As landed, the mirror in `patches/` carries these as `0008`/`0012` and\n`0009`/`0010` respectively — see `patches/MANIFEST.md` for the full 12-patch\nmap.)*\n\n| Patch | Content | Upstream destination |\n|---|---|---|\n| `patches/0008-*` + `patches/0012-*` | Oracle admission for block-FP8 fused-MoE on gfx1151 + fp8→bf16 in-kernel upcast in the fused-MoE Triton kernel (the #52970 pattern applied to MoE) + `FN_FP8_MOE` kill-switch + a loud log line at admission; plus the same upcast in the block-scaled **linear** Triton kernel (`FN_FP8_LINEAR`), without which the dense projections still hand fp8 to `tl.dot` | PR to vllm-project/vllm, referencing #52970 |\n| `patches/0009-*` + `patches/0010-*` | The `amd/` PLE port: mmap wiring (5 sites mirroring `nvidia/ple_layer.py`), the FP8 embedding stack (`Qwen4ExpPLEFp8EmbeddingMethod`, gather-time dequant, `weight_scale` interception) the AMD tree lacks entirely, `ple_mmap.py` relocated to `common/` | PR against #54129's head branch (its author has no gfx1151 hardware) |\n\n## 3. Method and code lifted from the community (per the innovation ledger)\n\n| Source | License | What | Mode |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm](https://github.com/AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm) @ `a8f620d` | Apache-2.0 | Patch-overlay discipline (MANIFEST + verify + 12 packaging invariants, extended); host orchestration shape (husk-reaping, ray pool caps, 2-GPU gate, ExecStopPost); env doctrine (PYTHONHASHSEED=0, expandable_segments, HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1, caches off tmpfs, ray env-prefix propagation); instruments `ds4_synctrace.py`/`ds4_expert_union.py`/`ds4_offload_batch.py` → adapted as `fn_*` with notices | copy + adapt |\n| [kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes](https://github.com/kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes) @ `23cb726` | MIT | Container recipe shape (`Dockerfile.ubuntu-repoamd`): Ubuntu 24.04 + AMD stable wheels + vLLM from source at arbitrary ref | adapt with notice |\n| kyuz0 toolbox QA docs | no license | Release-gate *method* only (log-grep lexicon, frontier-logit equivalence, depth-regression rule) | method only, no code |\n| [hellas-ai/nix-strix-halo](https://github.com/hellas-ai/nix-strix-halo) @ `f0f2048` | **no license** | Flake **input only** — nothing copied. NCCL/RCCL tuning *values* read as data. Its `tuning` module is explicitly forbidden (would fight our 128 GiB GTT ceiling). Its pair-bench client's `prefill_mean_s` is a TTFT duplicate — we ship our own client. | input use only |\n| llama.cpp-lane research (Nathan, EngramHalo) | MIT / research notes | Silicon facts (int4 2.03×, no fp8 unit, LLC no-allocate, wave32-native WMMA), q8_0-KV > fp8-KV, MoE-wants-large-ubatch, MTP k=3 prediction for 1-layer MTP, load-phase page-cache transient | knowledge |\n\n## 4. What is deliberately NOT imported\n\n- **RDMA/tbv anything** (GPL boundary + excluded scope; TCP is the transport of record).\n- **aiter** (no CK build for RDNA; its Triton-only path unproven on gfx1151 for our kernels; revisit post-first-light).\n- **nix-strix-halo `.nix` code** (no license), **kyuz0 toolbox shell scripts** (no license on those two repos — method only).\n- **ROCm 10** (no torch wheels exist for gfx1151; rocBLAS solution-index breakage documented).\n- **Community W4A16/AWQ quants** of this model (they quantize attention + GDN — exactly what the vendor kept precise).\n- **torchaudio** (caps torch at 2.11; not needed).\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987964531},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dfa95e2f30c54781ae9ee1b3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Third-party code and licenses\n\nThird-party sources are **fetched at pinned revisions at build time, not\nredistributed here** — what this repository itself ships is at most a\nderivative patch against them (each patch is licensed like the code it\nmodifies). Original code in this repository is licensed under\n[Apache-2.0](LICENSE). No GPL code enters this tree (the RDMA transport\nsubtree of the reference implementation is excluded from scope entirely).\n\n| Component | Upstream | License | What this repo ships |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| vLLM (+ PR #53896, #54129 content) | github.com/vllm-project/vllm; fork base `8e4e036` | Apache-2.0 | Derivative patches under `patches/`, mirrored as commits on github.com/mecattaf/vllm branch `flashnext`; provenance per file in `patches/MANIFEST.md` |\n| Cherry-picked open PRs #46012 #40963 #51511 #46110 | github.com/vllm-project/vllm pull requests | Apache-2.0 | Carried as fork commits with `Cherry-picked-from:` trailers; nothing redistributed here |\n| ds4-vllm instruments and discipline | github.com/AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ `a8f620d` | Apache-2.0 | Adapted copies under `container/rootfs/` (`fn_synctrace.py`, `fn_expert_union.py`, `fn_offload_batch.py`) retaining upstream notice headers; the packaging-test discipline reimplemented in `tests/` |\n| amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes container recipe | github.com/kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes @ `23cb726` | MIT | `container/Containerfile` is an adaptation; MIT notice retained in that file's header |\n| nix-strix-halo | github.com/hellas-ai/nix-strix-halo @ `f0f2048` | no license published | Consumed as a Nix flake input only; nothing redistributed, nothing copied |\n| AMD ROCm wheels (torch/triton/vision, rocm 7.14.0) | repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch | per-wheel licenses | Fetched at container build; nothing redistributed |\n\n**Model weights** (`Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8`) are not included and are\ngoverned by their own license on Hugging Face.\n----\nscripts:\nbuild-engine.sh\nmirror-substrate.sh\nreceipts-verify.py\nrun-smoke.sh\nstage-weights-both.sh\nstage-weights.sh\nverify-fork.sh\n\ntests:\ntest_repo_invariants.py\n----\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# In-container smoke: platform identity, fp8 storage+cast, model registry\n# resolution, and oracle admission — the cheap questions that must be\n# answered before any weight byte moves. Writes results/receipts/smoke.json.\nset -euo pipefail\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nOUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/smoke.json\"\n\npodman run --rm --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri \\\n  --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host \\\n  -v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\" \"$IMAGE\" python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, time, traceback\nr = {\"step\": \"smoke\", \"status\": \"pass\", \"ts\": time.strftime(\"%FT%T\"), \"data\": {}}\ndef try_(name, fn):\n    try:\n        r[\"data\"][name] = fn()\n    except Exception as e:\n        r[\"data\"][name] = f\"FAIL: {e.__class__.__name__}: {e}\"\n        r[\"status\"] = \"fail\"\n        traceback.print_exc()\n\ndef arch():\n    from vllm.platforms import rocm\n    return {\"gcn_arch\": rocm._GCN_ARCH, \"on_cdna\": rocm.on_cdna(),\n            \"supports_fp8_stock_predicate\": rocm.on_cdna() or rocm.on_rdna4()}\ndef fp8_cast():\n    import torch\n    x = torch.zeros(4, dtype=torch.float8_e4m3fn, device=\"cuda\")\n    y = (x.to(torch.bfloat16) + 1).sum().item()\n    return {\"e4m3fn_alloc_and_cast\": y == 4.0}\ndef registry():\n    from vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry\n    archs = ModelRegistry.get_supported_archs()\n    return {\"model_arch_registered\": \"Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration\" in archs}\ndef aperture():\n    return {\"ttm_pages_limit\": int(open(\n        \"/sys/module/ttm/parameters/pages_limit\").read().strip())}\ndef admission():\n    # The patched oracle must admit the block-FP8 scheme on this GPU.\n    from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.experts.triton_moe import TritonExperts\n    from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.utils.quant_utils import (\n        kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym)\n    ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(\n        kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym) \\\n        if hasattr(TritonExperts, \"_supports_quant_scheme\") else (False, \"no hook\")\n    return {\"fp8_block_moe_admitted\": bool(ok), \"reason\": str(why)}\n\ntry_(\"arch\", arch)\ntry_(\"fp8_cast\", fp8_cast)\ntry_(\"registry\", registry)\ntry_(\"aperture\", aperture)\ntry_(\"admission\", admission)\njson.dump(r, open(\"/results/receipts/smoke.json\", \"w\"), indent=1)\nprint(json.dumps(r, indent=1))\nPY\necho \"smoke receipt: $OUT\"\npython3 -c \"import json,sys; sys.exit(0 if json.load(open('$OUT'))['status']=='pass' else 1)\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987964531},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Next, check the packaging tests (tests/test_repo_invariants.py), scripts/build-engine.sh (does it exist? it's listed under scripts), and the evidence file kyuz0-rocm10.md. Also, check whether the rootfs module is expected: according to IMPORTS, `container/rootfs/` holds copies adapted from fn_synctrace.py, fn_expert_union.py, and fn_offload_batch.py. But I can only touch container/ and results/receipts/. Wait — IMPORTS states these files are placed under container/rootfs/. I need to create them. They are adaptations of ds4-vllm's instruments, retaining the upstream notification header. I don't have ds4-vllm on hand, but I can create a reasonable fn_* module. Hmm — but maybe the test suite verifies their existence? Let me read tests/test_repo_invariants.py.\n\nAlso check whether scripts/build-engine.sh exists (maybe for the nix lane). Additionally, check podman's images and the wheel cache.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_78435d2c965d497b98f2ba62","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && cat tests/test_repo_invariants.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0a0bac00e6b8490ca2ec0847","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && sed -n '1,80p' specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":5120,"output":362,"cacheRead":10496,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":210,"totalTokens":15978,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787987964536,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f07a2d95-a76e-45c3-b4d7-4ea702bfb16a","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_78435d2c965d497b98f2ba62","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Repo packaging invariants — the offline half of the discipline.\n\nModeled on ds4-vllm's test_patchset_packaging.py (Apache-2.0), extended:\nnew-file line counts are audited too (the upstream suite skipped them and\n3 of its 12 MANIFEST counts drifted).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport unittest\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n\nclass RepoInvariants(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_license_is_apache2(self):\n        text = (ROOT / \"LICENSE\").read_text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Apache License\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"Version 2.0\", text)\n\n    def test_no_gpl_text_in_tree(self):\n        needle = \"GNU GENERAL \" + \"PUBLIC LICENSE\"  # avoid self-match\n        for path in ROOT.rglob(\"*\"):\n            if path.is_dir() or \".git\" in path.parts \\\n                    or \"__pycache__\" in path.parts:\n                continue\n            # Evidence dossiers may QUOTE license headers they inspected.\n            if \"evidence\" in path.parts or path.name == \"test_repo_invariants.py\":\n                continue\n            if path.suffix in {\".safetensors\", \".gguf\"}:\n                continue\n            try:\n                text = path.read_text(errors=\"ignore\")\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n            self.assertNotIn(needle, text, f\"GPL text found in {path}\")\n\n    def test_no_secret_material(self):\n        patterns = [re.compile(p) for p in\n                    (r\"BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY\", r\"hf_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}\",\n                     r\"ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}\", r\"AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}\")]\n        for path in ROOT.rglob(\"*\"):\n            if path.is_dir() or \".git\" in path.parts \\\n                    or \"__pycache__\" in path.parts:\n                continue\n            try:\n                text = path.read_text(errors=\"ignore\")\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n            for pat in patterns:\n                self.assertIsNone(pat.search(text),\n                                  f\"secret-like material in {path}: {pat.pattern}\")\n\n    def test_spec_artifacts_exist(self):\n        self.assertTrue((ROOT / \"specs/flashnext/spec.md\").is_file())\n        trace = json.loads((ROOT / \"specs/flashnext/trace.json\").read_text())\n        self.assertEqual(trace[\"schemaVersion\"], 1)\n        self.assertTrue(\n            (ROOT / \"specs/flashnext/contracts/trace.schema.json\").is_file())\n\n    def test_evidence_dossiers_present(self):\n        dossiers = list((ROOT / \"specs/flashnext/evidence\").glob(\"*.md\"))\n        self.assertGreaterEqual(len(dossiers), 7)\n\n    def test_worklist_shape_and_hygiene(self):\n        wl_path = ROOT / \"silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"\n        wl = json.loads(wl_path.read_text())\n        self.assertEqual(wl[\"schemaVersion\"], 1)\n        self.assertTrue(wl[\"tasks\"])\n        raw = wl_path.read_text()\n        # Runtime hub downloads are forbidden estate-wide.\n        self.assertNotIn(\"-hf \", raw)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"hf download\", raw)\n        # Model-family names never enter worklist bytes (lint L16 mirror).\n        for banned in (\"qwen\", \"llama\", \"deepseek\", \"claude\", \"opus\"):\n            self.assertNotIn(banned, raw.lower(),\n                             f\"banned token '{banned}' in worklist bytes\")\n        # Every implementation task carries executable acceptance.\n        for task in wl[\"tasks\"]:\n            if task.get(\"kind\") == \"implementation\":\n                self.assertTrue(task.get(\"acceptanceCriteria\"),\n                                f\"{task['id']} has no acceptance criteria\")\n\n    def test_scripts_are_syntax_clean(self):\n        for sh in (ROOT / \"scripts\").glob(\"*.sh\"):\n            subprocess.run([\"bash\", \"-n\", str(sh)], check=True)\n        for sh in (ROOT / \"host\").rglob(\"*.sh\"):\n            subprocess.run([\"bash\", \"-n\", str(sh)], check=True)\n        for py in (ROOT / \"scripts\").glob(\"*.py\"):\n            subprocess.run([\"python3\", \"-m\", \"py_compile\", str(py)],\n                           check=True)\n\n    def test_receipts_verify_runs_clean(self):\n        proc = subprocess.run(\n            [\"python3\", str(ROOT / \"scripts/receipts-verify.py\")],\n            capture_output=True, text=True)\n        self.assertIn(proc.returncode, (0,),\n                      f\"receipts-verify failed:\\n{proc.stdout}{proc.stderr}\")\n\n    def test_notices_cover_the_import_manifest(self):\n        notices = (ROOT / \"THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\").read_text()\n        for needle in (\"vllm-project/vllm\", \"AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm\",\n                       \"amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes\", \"nix-strix-halo\"):\n            self.assertIn(needle, notices)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987973984},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0a0bac00e6b8490ca2ec0847","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# kyuz0 lineage — ROCm 10.0 update (2026-08-28) and the container-base decision\n\nInvestigated 2026-08-28. Analysis-only; no working tree was modified. All three\nclones were `git fetch origin`'d; every claim below carries a file:line or a\nliteral command output.\n\nGrades: **[S]** read from source · **[M]** measured (command output) · **[CL]** claimed by docs, unverified.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Headline\n\nkyuz0 did ship a **ROCm 10.0** migration today — but **only for the llama.cpp / ds4\n(GGUF) toolboxes**. The **vLLM lineage was not touched today and cannot be moved to\nROCm 10 right now**, because the wheel index that build auto-discovers from\n(`repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/`) tops out at **rocm7.14.0**. There is a newer\n`vllm-therock-gfx1151` image than the one ds4-vllm pins, but it is **ROCm 7.14 +\nvLLM 0.28.0**, not ROCm 10, and it is a **different distro and build method** than\nthe pinned digest.\n\nSo the campaign premise \"pin a base that has ROCm 10 + a vllm close to the PR\nmerge-base\" is **not currently satisfiable from kyuz0's registry**. Those are two\ndifferent image families.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Fetch results and what landed\n\n### 1.1 Fetch output [M]\n\n```\n$ cd /home/tom/Downloads/amd-strix-halo-toolboxes && git fetch origin\n(no new refs; local main already at origin/main)\norigin  https://github.com/kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-toolboxes (fetch)\n\n$ cd /home/tom/Downloads/strix-halo-ds4-toolbox && git fetch origin\nFrom https://github.com/kyuz0/strix-halo-ds4-toolbox\n   10e9941..43a7fa5  main -> origin/main\n * [new tag]         cockpit-v2026.8.28.1814 -> cockpit-v2026.8.28.1814\n * [new tag]         cockpit-v2026.8.28.1707 -> cockpit-v2026.8.28.1707\n\n$ cd /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-kyuz0 && git fetch origin\nFrom https://github.com/kyuz0/ds4\n   971110a..7eb2058  perf/rocm-gfx1151-mmq-kernel-lab -> origin/perf/rocm-gfx1151-mmq-kernel-lab\n```\n\nNote `ds4-kyuz0` tracks **only** `perf/rocm-gfx1151-mmq-kernel-lab` from\n`origin` (`kyuz0/ds4.git`); it also carries a second remote `up` →\n`../ds4-antirez`. [M]\n\n### 1.2 Commit volume [M]\n\n```\n$ git log --all --since=2026-08-21 --oneline | wc -l   (and today's window)\namd-strix-halo-toolboxes    7d=7   today=2\nstrix-halo-ds4-toolbox      7d=9   today=7\nds4-kyuz0                   7d=53  today=13\n```\n\n### 1.3 `amd-strix-halo-toolboxes` — origin/main, last 7 days [M]\n\n| Commit | Date (iso) | Subject |\n|---|---|---|\n| `9ff3c5e7791ce70d89a1d8fa2ffcd54268b5f7b4` | 2026-08-28 08:16:02 +0100 | Retire deprecated ROCm and AMDVLK toolboxes |\n| `d3cef36e858bd97a780e470fa5ceba5198638788` | 2026-08-28 08:06:56 +0100 | **Replace stable ROCm 7.14 toolbox with ROCm 10.0** |\n| `aa13f7e4aa13d6590769ae4ffe182add3795c4c2` | 2026-08-27 12:04:03 +0100 | Update Qwen3.8 Flash Next toolbox PR source |\n| `dcda4fcfbf186878162d120b4a0c3a529834b30e` | 2026-08-27 08:45:42 +0100 | Fix Qwen3.8 Flash Next toolbox source |\n| `9a6edb9074e2e8cd60c076dbb17b1ee1610b2429` | 2026-08-26 16:06:08 +0100 | Add experimental Qwen3.8 Flash Next ROCm toolbox |\n| `c8777f2aab3997b2f1ec653a2c5c27b2b1fdc2d3` | 2026-08-26 11:26:22 +0100 | feat: add ROCm 7.14 performance toolbox |\n| `e3c240aa2caf93e16926a68ce6dfb2a2ff7d7c72` | 2026-08-24 09:02:11 +0100 | feat: enable ROCmI4 W4A4 in ROCmFPX toolbox |\n\n### 1.4 `strix-halo-ds4-toolbox` — origin/main, last 7 days [M]\n\n| Commit | Date (iso) | Subject |\n|---|---|---|\n| `43a7fa5b06ba6147c8f82963250c1d7c43074b29` | 2026-08-28 18:14:02 +0000 | chore(cockpit): bump version to 2026.8.28.1814 |\n| `a3731de89dd32c42a21cb9d3a51f17f9c0c1f94f` | 2026-08-28 18:10:13 +0100 | fix |\n| `b332244dd2634f1e085fcd969450f36dbf1f1a97` | 2026-08-28 17:07:28 +0000 | chore(cockpit): bump version to 2026.8.28.1707 |\n| `7e23f647d634184fd8f873b833a3abda16c6072f` | 2026-08-28 18:07:15 +0100 | deprecation of cockpit |\n| `10e99417cc7c24011a2c2809abf1ea230b2d8c5a` | 2026-08-28 11:57:55 +0000 | chore(cockpit): bump version to 2026.8.28.1157 |\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987973984},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so let's check the state of the podman image, wheel cache, and scripts/build-engine.sh (might be from a separate lane — check if it's already committed). Also check the triton version in the wheel cache: per steering it's triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0.\n\nAlso check receipts-verify.py to understand the expected receipt format.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_83c567448c9c4ff394f88ca5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/tom/.cache/flashnext-wheels/ 2>/dev/null; podman images 2>/dev/null | head -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ce528d7673d849efb09382d9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && sed -n '1,120p' scripts/receipts-verify.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":4335,"output":220,"cacheRead":14720,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":83,"totalTokens":19275,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787987973988,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e936f161-b26d-4439-8cf8-cd00e95ee9f4","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_83c567448c9c4ff394f88ca5","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 527140\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 tom users      4096 Aug 29 08:09 .\ndrwx------ 62 tom users      4096 Aug 29 08:41 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 tom users 193676721 Aug 29 08:09 torch-2.13.0+rocm7.14.0-cp312-cp312-linux_x86_64.whl\n-rw-r--r--  1 tom users   1116841 Aug 29 08:09 torchvision-0.28.0+rocm7.14.0-cp312-cp312-linux_x86_64.whl\n-rw-r--r--  1 tom users 344974357 Aug 29 08:09 triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0-cp312-cp312-linux_x86_64.whl\nREPOSITORY                TAG         IMAGE ID      CREATED            SIZE\nlocalhost/flashnext       dev         1b5fda5f0529  12 minutes ago     18.2 GB\n<none>                    <none>      f8d4aef8a242  38 minutes ago     17.2 GB\n<none>                    <none>      75dc4f8e3939  55 minutes ago     6.41 GB\n<none>                    <none>      f45d73a4faef  About an hour ago  5.99 GB\n<none>                    <none>      3d2544115dec  About an hour ago  614 MB\ndocker.io/library/ubuntu  24.04       a6f81fb630d5  11 days ago        80.7 MB\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987980436},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ce528d7673d849efb09382d9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate every overnight receipt under results/receipts/.\n\nA receipt is one JSON object: {\"step\": str, \"status\": \"pass\"|\"fail\",\n\"ts\": str, \"data\": {...}}. Missing receipts are legal (the step has not\nrun); a present receipt must be well-formed, and hard bounds are enforced\nper step. Any violation exits 2 — this is the ladder gate that makes the\novernight claims graded rather than narrated.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nRECEIPTS = ROOT / \"results\" / \"receipts\"\n\n# Per-step hard bounds: step-name prefix -> checker(data) -> error or None.\ndef _residency(d):\n    for rank, gib in (d.get(\"gtt_gib_per_rank\") or {}).items():\n        if gib > 80:\n            return f\"rank {rank} GTT {gib} GiB exceeds the 80 GiB bound\"\n    if d.get(\"table_gpu_resident_bytes\", 0) != 0:\n        return \"table has GPU-resident bytes; the mmap path is not engaged\"\n    if not d.get(\"read_after_warmed_decode\", False):\n        return \"residency was not read after a warmed decode\"\n    return None\n\ndef _tp2(d):\n    if not d.get(\"byte_identical_repeat\", False):\n        return \"greedy repeat was not byte-identical\"\n    return None\n\ndef _weights(d):\n    if d.get(\"shards\", 0) < 131:\n        return f\"only {d.get('shards')} shards staged\"\n    return None\n\ndef _bench(d):\n    if d.get(\"loads_per_arm\", 0) < 3:\n        return \"fewer than 3 loads per arm\"\n    if not d.get(\"counterbalanced\", False):\n        return \"arms were not counterbalanced\"\n    return None\n\ndef _context(d):\n    ratio = d.get(\"decode_ratio_vs_short_context\")\n    if ratio is not None and ratio < 0.9:\n        return f\"full-context decode ratio {ratio} below the 0.9 bound\"\n    return None\n\ndef _smoke(d):\n    ap = (d.get(\"aperture\") or {}).get(\"ttm_pages_limit\")\n    if ap is not None and ap != 33554432:\n        return f\"aperture {ap} diverges from the 33554432-page ceiling\"\n    return None\n\nBOUNDS = {\n    \"residency\": _residency,\n    \"tp2\": _tp2,\n    \"weights\": _weights,\n    \"bench\": _bench,\n    \"context\": _context,\n    \"smoke\": _smoke,\n}\n\ndef _handoff_patch_ok() -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"When the catalog patch exists it must parse as a git patch.\"\"\"\n    import subprocess\n    patch = ROOT / \"handoff\" / \"catalog-row.patch\"\n    if not patch.is_file():\n        return None\n    proc = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"apply\", \"--stat\", str(patch)],\n                          capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if proc.returncode != 0:\n        return f\"handoff/catalog-row.patch does not parse: {proc.stderr.strip()}\"\n    return None\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    bad = 0\n    err = _handoff_patch_ok()\n    if err:\n        print(f\"receipts-verify: {err}\")\n        bad += 1\n    if not RECEIPTS.is_dir():\n        print(\"receipts-verify: no receipts directory; nothing ran\")\n        return 2 if bad else 0\n    seen = 0\n    for path in sorted(RECEIPTS.glob(\"*.json\")):\n        seen += 1\n        try:\n            r = json.loads(path.read_text())\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n            print(f\"receipts-verify: {path.name}: invalid JSON: {e}\")\n            bad += 1\n            continue\n        for key in (\"step\", \"status\", \"ts\"):\n            if key not in r:\n                print(f\"receipts-verify: {path.name}: missing '{key}'\")\n                bad += 1\n        if r.get(\"status\") == \"fail\":\n            print(f\"receipts-verify: {path.name}: step '{r.get('step')}' FAILED\")\n            bad += 1\n        for prefix, check in BOUNDS.items():\n            if str(r.get(\"step\", \"\")).startswith(prefix):\n                err = check(r.get(\"data\") or {})\n                if err:\n                    print(f\"receipts-verify: {path.name}: {err}\")\n                    bad += 1\n    print(f\"receipts-verify: {seen} receipts checked, {bad} violations\")\n    return 2 if bad else 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987980436},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — the flashnext:dev image exists (created 12 minutes ago, 18.2GB) — probably from a previous attempt's build... wait no, 12 minutes ago? The previous attempt was earlier, and maybe the campaign was re-run. Either way, the image exists and the layer cache is warm.\n\nThe previous attempt's container/ files are lost (not committed). container/ needs to be written from scratch. But wait — the image was built 12 minutes ago from a Containerfile that no longer exists. Layer cache: if I write a Containerfile with identical instructions, podman will reuse the cached layers, making the build fast. But I don't know the exact contents of the previous Containerfile. The cache matches on instruction text, so different text → rebuild. Hmm, but steering says \"re-running build.sh should be fast thanks to the layer cache.\" If the instructions differ even slightly, the cache is broken. There's risk. But a full rebuild takes 64 minutes.\n\nAlternative: maybe the previous attempt's files are still around somewhere — stash? git stash list? dangling blobs? Let me check git fsck dangling and reflog. The previous attempt didn't commit anything, but it might have stashed or left files somewhere else. I'll also check the podman build history — does `podman history` show the commands? Actually, podman inspect on the image shows the config but not the Dockerfile instructions. The intermediate layers (unnamed images) exist. `podman inspect` on intermediate images shows the CreatedBy commands, which might reveal the exact RUN strings, but not the full Containerfile text.\n\nLet me check git stash, dangling commits/blobs, and also other worktrees in the campaign directory — the previous attempt was probably on the same worktree path. I'll also check the build metadata in ~/.local/share/containers or podman.\n\nActually — the build was 12 minutes ago?? The image's CREATED is 12 minutes ago. The steering comment timestamp is 07:11 UTC. The current time is? Let me check the date. If the previous attempt built very recently and didn't commit the files... maybe the attempt is still running? No, this is a new stateless attempt.\n\nHmm, wait — maybe the previous attempt wrote container files somewhere else. Like directly into the repo directory instead of the worktree? The worktree path is specified in the brief. Let me search the filesystem for a Containerfile named flashnext.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_45e048ee36f04d489b39eb93","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"date; cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && git stash list; git fsck --dangling 2>/dev/null | head; git log --oneline tally-work/flashnext-a871de4d3faa/container-recipe -3"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_06bafda2a75d4f358b0fa68a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"find /home/tom/.local/state/tally /home/tom/.local/share/tally /tmp -name 'Containerfile*' -o -name 'build.sh' -path '*container*' 2>/dev/null | head; ls /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1955,"output":732,"cacheRead":18944,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":522,"totalTokens":21631,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787987980441,"responseId":"chatcmpl-063e541f-2f56-462d-a4b4-7899d242fce7","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_45e048ee36f04d489b39eb93","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sat Aug 29 09:19:59 AM CEST 2026\ndangling commit 5ee20022611be510f1105bbb59fc05cdd0192faa\ndangling blob cd201afb4b2126b9c8466d56a12a23e553f4d57e\ndangling commit d89f338f1e74622415022809f9becb28b73f86fa\ndangling blob f483a1b85f6931a5c4d901c61e2c52726386fc07\na428fee handoff: staging complete, campaign launches attended-by-daylight not overnight\nf6db565 receipts: weights staged on both nodes (131 shards, 185563801379 bytes each)\nd62bd2f handoff: OVERSEER-LAUNCH refresh — routing read order, overseer owns the arm, weights pre-staging state, NCCL discipline\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988007216},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_06bafda2a75d4f358b0fa68a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-tom-mecattaf-notes-qwen-next/c4262a6d-5cde-494b-9143-685dd896a84f/scratchpad/estate-scratch/container/build.sh\n/tmp/claude-1000/-home-tom-Downloads/6ad7b83e-2b9c-4a50-9cda-0518c5146e92/scratchpad/AlexKGwyn_ds4-vllm/container/build.sh\n/tmp/claude-1000/-home-tom-Downloads/6ad7b83e-2b9c-4a50-9cda-0518c5146e92/scratchpad/ds4-vllm-public/container/build.sh\n/tmp/claude-1000/-home-tom-mecattaf-dotfiles/98bf94ac-8d65-45fc-a15a-e29fa6e848e2/scratchpad/ds4/container/build.sh\n/tmp/claude-1000/-home-tom-mecattaf-dotfiles/d50d27cb-b3ba-4f7e-b7ec-149df36d76e7/scratchpad/notes-filter/references/archive/april-agency-refs/wayland-tools/gtk4-layer-shell/test/Containerfile\ncontainer-recipe\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988007216},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's a dangling commit in the worktree's git repository. Let's investigate it—there might be an attempt at a previous commit (possibly lost due to a reset). Let me display it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_10d3cfad94c34190be32ab53","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && git log --stat 5ee20022611be510f1105bbb59fc05cdd0192faa -2 | head -60; echo ====; git log --stat d89f338f1e74622415022809f9becb28b73f86fa -2 | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1785,"output":199,"cacheRead":20480,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":40,"totalTokens":22464,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988007221,"responseId":"chatcmpl-bf22bdd6-26ea-40d4-912a-8f514006a307","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_10d3cfad94c34190be32ab53","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"commit 5ee20022611be510f1105bbb59fc05cdd0192faa\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sat Aug 29 09:11:20 2026 +0200\n\n    container: recipe for flashnext:dev — pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\n    \n    Containerfile (Ubuntu 24.04, py3.12 venv at /opt/venv), shape adapted from\n    kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes Dockerfile.ubuntu-repoamd (MIT notice in\n    header, per THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md):\n    \n    - substrate pinned from repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch: torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0,\n      torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0, triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (the exact\n      companion pip resolves for torch 2.13.0), rocm-sdk-devel for the HIP compiler;\n      torchaudio omitted, not downgraded\n    - finding: the generic torch/torchvision wheels ship no device kernels — first launch\n      dies hipErrorInvalidImage until amd-torch-device-gfx1151 / amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151\n      / rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151 are installed; pinned too\n    - mecattaf/vllm branch flashnext cloned --depth 1 and built from source\n      (editable, --no-build-isolation, PYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH=gfx1151); a bind-mounted\n      checkout over /opt/vllm plus host ccache/pip caches (build.sh) make one-line\n      patch rebuilds incremental and the image enterable for edit-and-restart\n    - container/rootfs/ overlay COPYs into site-packages (fn_ instruments land importable)\n    - /opt/flashnext/build-info.json records fork commit, torch, triton, build time\n    \n    build.sh: packaging tests first, podman build flashnext:dev, receipt\n    results/receipts/build.json (fail status on any error). Attempt-2 fix per the\n    machine diagnosis: host ccache/pip cache defaults moved from $REPO_ROOT/.build/\n    to ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/flashnext/{ccache,pip} so the worktree never\n    gains untracked files outside container/ and results/receipts/; overrides\n    FN_CCACHE_DIR / FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR and the podman --volume wiring unchanged.\n    No log files are written into the repo. Receipt banked: status pass, wall-clock\n    839 s; image verified on the GPU — kernels launch, fp8 storage cast finite,\n    Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration registered, block-FP8 MoE admitted on gfx1151.\n\n container/Containerfile     | 147 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n container/build.sh          | 118 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n container/rootfs/.keep      |   3 +\n results/receipts/build.json |  14 +++++\n 4 files changed, 282 insertions(+)\n\ncommit a428fee66b83d95682b418d5fdb4d975068e66ab\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sat Aug 29 08:00:39 2026 +0200\n\n    handoff: staging complete, campaign launches attended-by-daylight not overnight\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhApDR1sd6CHYstMF6ZPAv\n\n handoff/OVERSEER-LAUNCH.md | 27 ++++++++++++---------------\n 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)\n====\ncommit d89f338f1e74622415022809f9becb28b73f86fa\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sat Aug 29 09:08:38 2026 +0200\n\n    container: recipe for flashnext:dev — pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\n    \n    Containerfile (Ubuntu 24.04, py3.12 venv at /opt/venv), shape adapted from\n    kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes Dockerfile.ubuntu-repoamd (MIT notice in\n    header, per THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md):\n    \n    - substrate pinned from repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch: torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0,\n      torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0, triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (the exact\n      companion pip resolves for torch 2.13.0; the fork's upcast gate keys triton < 3.8,\n      recorded), rocm-sdk-devel for the HIP compiler; torchaudio omitted, not downgraded\n    - finding: the generic torch/torchvision wheels ship no device kernels — first launch\n      dies hipErrorInvalidImage until amd-torch-device-gfx1151 / amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151\n      / rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151 are installed (torch loads them from torch/.kpack/); pinned too\n    - mecattaf/vllm branch flashnext cloned --depth 1 and built from source\n      (editable, --no-build-isolation, PYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH=gfx1151); a bind-mounted\n      checkout over /opt/vllm plus host ccache/pip caches (build.sh) make one-line\n      patch rebuilds incremental and the image enterable for edit-and-restart\n    - container/rootfs/ overlay COPYs into site-packages (fn_ instruments land importable)\n    - /opt/flashnext/build-info.json records fork commit, torch, triton, build time\n    \n    build.sh: packaging tests first, podman build flashnext:dev, receipt\n    results/receipts/build.json (fail status on any error). Receipt banked: status\n    pass, wall-clock 839 s; image verified on the GPU — kernels launch, fp8 storage\n    cast finite, Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration registered, block-FP8 MoE admitted\n    on gfx1151.\n\n container/Containerfile     | 147 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n container/build.sh          | 110 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n container/rootfs/.keep      |   3 +\n results/receipts/build.json |  14 +++++\n 4 files changed, 274 insertions(+)\n\ncommit a428fee66b83d95682b418d5fdb4d975068e66ab\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sat Aug 29 08:00:39 2026 +0200\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988012509},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A previous attempt actually committed (dangling commit 5ee2002, 09:11:20 — just 8 minutes ago), but afterwards the branch got reset (probably by the harness before ownership verification, or the commit was orphaned). The dangling commit has the full work done and matches the existing image (the image was created at 09:11 or so? Actually the image shows \"created 12 minutes ago\" ≈ 09:07, which matches the attempt-2 build).\n\nWait — but according to the steering, the previous attempt terminated without committing. There are 2 dangling commits (09:08 and 09:11) — looks like the previous attempt committed and then something reset the branch (probably the tally driver did the reset, or the agent ran `git reset`). Either way, cleanest reconcile is: restore the worktree from dangling commit 5ee2002 (latest), confirm acceptance passes, commit on the branch.\n\nBut wait — the commit is already dangling. Can I just point the branch at 5ee2002? It contains exactly the right files. Its parent is a428fee (current branch HEAD). So `git reset --hard 5ee2002` restores it. But should I re-verify the acceptance criteria and re-run build.sh? Per steering, re-run will be fast due to layer cache. The receipt already exists with pass status. Acceptance criteria only require bash -n and grep — fast.\n\nHowever: one concern — the commit message says triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0, but the fork's upcast gate depends on triton < 3.8. Hmm, this is a concern noted within the commit. But the acceptance test grep doesn't check triton. Also the goal says \"matching triton wheel from the vendor's stable index… (record the exact triton version resolved)\". In the warm cache triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0 is pre-downloaded, but… per the commit, pip resolved 3.8.0+git4cff872c. Hmm, but that's what was actually built and verified on GPU. Not a problem — reconcile with existing state, don't second-guess.\n\nAlso verify the receipt's content matches the image digest and so on. And confirm rootfs/.keep — goal says COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrumentation modules get placed. The commit only has .keep — no fn_ modules? In IMPORTS.md the fn_* instruments are placed under container/rootfs/. But that might be a separate task (fn instruments?). This task's conflict domain is container/ — the previous attempt only created .keep. Hmm, but IMPORTS says the adapted copies under container/rootfs/ retain the header. That might be a separate task. If COPY container/rootfs/ exists, it works even with just .keep. The judge graded the prior attempt as… the judge failed it purely on ownership verification (uncommitted changes), not on content. So the content is acceptable.\n\nDecision: restore via cherry-pick / reset to dangling commit 5ee2002? Branch currently points at a428fee, which is the commit's parent, so `git reset --hard 5ee2002...` will set the branch pointer there. This reproduces the \"commit the full result\" requirement. But is that considered \"my\" commit? The task says \"commit the complete result to the assigned branch\". Using the existing dangling commit preserves the prior work (the stateless reconcile instructions say \"inspect and preserve existing task work\").\n\nSafer alternative: checkout the files from the dangling commit into the worktree, inspect them, then create a fresh commit with the same message. But in that case, does the image's layer cache match the Containerfile contents? Yes, because the contents are identical (build.sh just does podman build, which will hit the cache anyway). Do I need to re-run build.sh? Acceptance criteria don't require build.sh execution, only syntax check and grep. Receipt already exists (status pass, ts). Re-running build.sh would rewrite the receipt with a new ts and digest — should be fast with cache, but takes a few minutes and risks flaky failures. The receipt inside the dangling commit was written by the actually-successful build. Restoring it as-is is most faithful.\n\nLet me inspect the files in the dangling commit first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"A previous attempt's complete work survives as dangling commits. Let me inspect the latest one before restoring it.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_388610c878e04eac92206dfe","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && git show 5ee2002:container/Containerfile"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9ce805e3afbf4059b0136808","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && git show 5ee2002:container/build.sh; echo ====; git show 5ee2002:results/receipts/build.json; echo ====; git show 5ee2002:container/rootfs/.keep; echo ====; git diff d89f338 5ee2002 --stat"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2662,"output":1187,"cacheRead":21504,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":957,"totalTokens":25353,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988012513,"responseId":"chatcmpl-fc40b4a6-832d-49c2-a0fd-168d47ebe1ea","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_388610c878e04eac92206dfe","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# flashnext:dev — the engine fork built from source at the exactly pinned wheel set\n# ============================================================================\n#\n# Recipe shape adapted from kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes,\n# `Dockerfile.ubuntu-repoamd` @ 23cb726, credited per THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.\n# That recipe is MIT licensed; the notice is retained here as required:\n#\n#   MIT License — Copyright (c) kyuz0 (amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes)\n#\n#   Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a\n#   copy of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"),\n#   to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation\n#   the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense,\n#   and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the\n#   Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n#\n#   The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in\n#   all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n#\n#   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n#   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n#   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n#   AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n#   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING\n#   FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER\n#   DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n#\n# What changed vs the donor recipe (per IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2):\n#   - torch is pinned to the fork's exact pin 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 from the AMD\n#     stable multi-arch index (the index tops out there; no ROCm 10 wheels\n#     exist for gfx1151 — specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md).\n#   - torchaudio is OMITTED; we drop the audio extra rather than downgrade\n#     torch to 2.11 (torchaudio capped kyuz0's auto-resolved set there).\n#   - the engine is the flashnext fork (mecattaf/vllm, branch flashnext),\n#     built from source for gfx1151, not a stock vLLM ref.\n#   - designed for overnight iteration: bind-mount a fork checkout over\n#     /opt/vllm and a host dir over /root/.ccache (see container/build.sh);\n#     the editable install then recompiles only what a one-line patch touched.\n#\n# Wheel provenance: the torch/triton/vision/rocm-sdk substrate comes ONLY\n# from the vendor stable index (spec F.11). Generic Python build tooling\n# (setuptools, wheel, packaging, setuptools-scm) and vLLM's upstream runtime\n# dependencies resolve from PyPI as upstream vLLM does; none of those is part\n# of the pinned substrate.\n\nFROM docker.io/ubuntu:24.04\n\nARG ROCM_WHL=https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/\n# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n# verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n# triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n# < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n# so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n# fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\nARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"\n# The from-source engine build needs the HIP compiler + cmake packages, which\n# the runtime wheels do not pull in; devel files merge into _rocm_sdk_core.\nARG ROCM_DEVEL_PIN=\"rocm-sdk-devel==7.14.0\"\n# The generic torch/torchvision wheels carry no device kernels; gfx1151 kernel\n# images ship as separate device packages (torch loads them from torch/.kpack/).\n# Without these the first kernel launch dies with hipErrorInvalidImage.\nARG DEVICE_PINS=\"amd-torch-device-gfx1151==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151==7.14.0\"\n\nENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n        python3.12 python3.12-venv python3.12-dev \\\n        git ca-certificates curl \\\n        build-essential cmake ninja-build ccache \\\n        cargo rustc libnuma-dev \\\n    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n\n# Python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv (pip arrives via ensurepip — no external fetch).\nRUN python3.12 -m venv /opt/venv\nENV VIRTUAL_ENV=/opt/venv \\\n    PATH=/opt/venv/bin:$PATH \\\n    PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=0 \\\n    PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1 \\\n    CCACHE_DIR=/root/.ccache \\\n    HOME=/root\n\n# Python build tooling (setuptools is served by the vendor index itself; the\n# rest is generic build-time tooling, not substrate).\nRUN pip install --index-url ${ROCM_WHL} --extra-index-url https://pypi.org/simple \\\n        setuptools wheel packaging \"setuptools-scm>=8.0\" setuptools-rust\n\n# ---- the pinned wheel substrate (vendor stable index only, spec F.11) ----\nRUN pip install --index-url ${ROCM_WHL} \\\n        ${TORCH_PIN} ${TORCHVISION_PIN} ${TRITON_PIN} ${ROCM_DEVEL_PIN} ${DEVICE_PINS}\n\n# ---- the engine fork, built from source for gfx1151 ----\nARG VLLM_REPO=https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm\nARG VLLM_BRANCH=flashnext\nENV VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=rocm \\\n    PYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH=gfx1151\n\n# If a host fork checkout is bind-mounted over /opt/vllm (build.sh -v), keep\n# it — that is the incremental-iteration path. Otherwise clone the baseline.\nRUN if [ ! -d /opt/vllm/.git ]; then \\\n        git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm /opt/vllm; \\\n    fi \\\n    && git -C /opt/vllm rev-parse HEAD > /opt/flashnext-fork-commit \\\n    && git -C /opt/vllm rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD >> /opt/flashnext-fork-commit\n\n# Editable, no build isolation: the build links against the venv's pinned\n# torch and never resolves build-system.requires (the fork's torch==2.11.0\n# build-system pin is therefore irrelevant here — IMPORTS.md section 1).\n# Build artifacts land inside /opt/vllm, so a bind-mounted checkout keeps\n# them across rebuilds and ccache (on PATH, auto-detected by vLLM's cmake)\n# recompiles only what changed.\nRUN pip install -e /opt/vllm --no-build-isolation\n\n# ---- the fn_ instrument overlay ----\n# Lands the instrument modules importable at the top level of site-packages.\nCOPY container/rootfs/ /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/\n\n# ---- build identity ----\nRUN mkdir -p /opt/flashnext && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, time, importlib.metadata as md\ndef ver(name):\n    try:\n        return md.version(name)\n    except md.PackageNotFoundError:\n        return \"unknown\"\nlines = open(\"/opt/flashnext-fork-commit\").read().splitlines()\ninfo = {\n    \"lane\": \"container\",\n    \"image\": \"flashnext:dev\",\n    \"fork_repo\": \"https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm\",\n    \"fork_commit\": lines[0],\n    \"fork_branch\": lines[1] if len(lines) > 1 else \"flashnext\",\n    \"torch\": md.version(\"torch\"),\n    \"torchvision\": md.version(\"torchvision\"),\n    \"triton\": md.version(\"triton\"),\n    \"rocm_sdk_core\": ver(\"rocm-sdk-core\"),\n    \"amd_torch_device_gfx1151\": ver(\"amd-torch-device-gfx1151\"),\n    \"gpu_target\": \"gfx1151\",\n    \"built_at\": time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z\"),\n}\njson.dump(info, open(\"/opt/flashnext/build-info.json\", \"w\"), indent=1)\nPY\nRUN cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json\n\nWORKDIR /opt/vllm\nCMD [\"bash\"]\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988041568},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9ce805e3afbf4059b0136808","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Container engine build — flashnext:dev (the ruling P4 container lane).\n#\n# Order per the task: packaging tests first, then the image build, then the\n# build receipt. Any error lands a receipt with status \"fail\" — the receipts\n# gate grades this step, so failure is recorded, never silent.\n#\n# Overnight-iteration hooks (see container/Containerfile header):\n#   FN_VLLM_SRC=/path/to/vllm-checkout   bind-mount the fork source over\n#                                        /opt/vllm; the editable install's\n#                                        build artifacts persist there, so a\n#                                        one-line patch rebuild recompiles\n#                                        only what changed.\n#   FN_CCACHE_DIR=/path/to/ccache        host compiler cache (default\n#                                        ~/.cache/flashnext/ccache — always\n#                                        OUTSIDE the repo, so the worktree\n#                                        stays clean), mounted at /root/.ccache.\n#   FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/pip        host pip cache (default\n#                                        ~/.cache/flashnext/pip), mounted at\n#                                        /root/.cache/pip.\n#   FN_IMAGE=name:tag                    image tag (default flashnext:dev).\n#\n# Enter the image for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild:\n#   podman run --rm -it --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri \\\n#     --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host \\\n#     -v \"$FN_VLLM_SRC:/opt/vllm\" flashnext:dev bash\n#   # inside: edit, then `pip install -e /opt/vllm --no-build-isolation`\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$REPO_ROOT\"\n\nIMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\"\nOUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/build.json\"\n# Host cache defaults live OUTSIDE the repository so nothing outside the\n# container/ and results/receipts/ write boundary is ever created or left\n# untracked in the worktree. Override with FN_CCACHE_DIR / FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR.\nHOST_CACHE_BASE=\"${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/flashnext\"\nCCACHE_DIR_HOST=\"${FN_CCACHE_DIR:-$HOST_CACHE_BASE/ccache}\"\nPIP_CACHE_HOST=\"${FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR:-$HOST_CACHE_BASE/pip}\"\n\nSTATUS=\"pass\"\nTORCH=\"\" TRITON=\"\" FORK_COMMIT=\"\" IMAGE_DIGEST=\"\"\nSTART_EPOCH=\"$(date +%s)\"\n\nwrite_receipt() {\n    local status=\"$1\"\n    local wall=$(( $(date +%s) - START_EPOCH ))\n    mkdir -p \"$(dirname \"$OUT\")\"\n    FN_STATUS=\"$status\" FN_TS=\"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" FN_WALL=\"$wall\" \\\n    FN_TORCH=\"$TORCH\" FN_TRITON=\"$TRITON\" FN_FORK=\"$FORK_COMMIT\" \\\n    FN_DIGEST=\"$IMAGE_DIGEST\" FN_IMAGE_NAME=\"$IMAGE\" python3 - \"$OUT\" <<'PY'\nimport json, os, sys\nr = {\n    \"step\": \"build\",\n    \"status\": os.environ[\"FN_STATUS\"],\n    \"ts\": os.environ[\"FN_TS\"],\n    \"data\": {\n        \"lane\": \"container\",\n        \"image\": os.environ[\"FN_IMAGE_NAME\"],\n        \"torch\": os.environ[\"FN_TORCH\"] or None,\n        \"triton\": os.environ[\"FN_TRITON\"] or None,\n        \"fork_commit\": os.environ[\"FN_FORK\"] or None,\n        \"image_digest\": os.environ[\"FN_DIGEST\"] or None,\n        \"wall_clock_s\": int(os.environ[\"FN_WALL\"]),\n    },\n}\njson.dump(r, open(sys.argv[1], \"w\"), indent=1)\nprint(f\"build receipt ({os.environ['FN_STATUS']}): {sys.argv[1]}\")\nPY\n}\n\non_error() {\n    echo \"container/build.sh: FAILED — writing fail receipt\" >&2\n    STATUS=\"fail\"\n    write_receipt \"fail\" || true\n    exit 1\n}\ntrap on_error ERR\n\necho \"==> packaging tests first\"\npython3 -m unittest discover -s \"$REPO_ROOT/tests\"\n\necho \"==> rootfs overlay stage (instruments land here when present)\"\nmkdir -p \"$REPO_ROOT/container/rootfs\"\n[ -e \"$REPO_ROOT/container/rootfs/.keep\" ] || touch \"$REPO_ROOT/container/rootfs/.keep\"\n\necho \"==> caches\"\nmkdir -p \"$CCACHE_DIR_HOST\" \"$PIP_CACHE_HOST\"\n\nBUILD_ARGS=(--tag \"$IMAGE\" --file container/Containerfile\n            --volume \"$CCACHE_DIR_HOST:/root/.ccache\"\n            --volume \"$PIP_CACHE_HOST:/root/.cache/pip\")\nif [ -n \"${FN_VLLM_SRC:-}\" ]; then\n    echo \"==> bind-mounting fork checkout: $FN_VLLM_SRC -> /opt/vllm\"\n    BUILD_ARGS+=(--volume \"$FN_VLLM_SRC:/opt/vllm\")\nfi\n\necho \"==> podman build $IMAGE\"\npodman build \"${BUILD_ARGS[@]}\" \"$REPO_ROOT\"\n\necho \"==> reading build identity from the image\"\nBUILD_INFO=\"$(podman run --rm --entrypoint /usr/bin/env \"$IMAGE\" \\\n    cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json)\"\necho \"$BUILD_INFO\"\nTORCH=\"$(echo \"$BUILD_INFO\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"torch\"])')\"\nTRITON=\"$(echo \"$BUILD_INFO\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"triton\"])')\"\nFORK_COMMIT=\"$(echo \"$BUILD_INFO\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"fork_commit\"])')\"\n\nIMAGE_DIGEST=\"$(podman inspect --format '{{.Digest}}' \"$IMAGE\" 2>/dev/null || true)\"\nif [ -z \"$IMAGE_DIGEST\" ]; then\n    # Local builds carry no registry digest; the image id is the stable name.\n    IMAGE_DIGEST=\"$(podman inspect --format '{{.Id}}' \"$IMAGE\")\"\nfi\n\nwrite_receipt \"$STATUS\"\npython3 -c \"import json,sys; sys.exit(0 if json.load(open('$OUT'))['status']=='pass' else 1)\"\necho \"==> flashnext:dev built; receipt: $OUT\"\n====\n{\n \"step\": \"build\",\n \"status\": \"pass\",\n \"ts\": \"2026-08-29T07:07:21Z\",\n \"data\": {\n  \"lane\": \"container\",\n  \"image\": \"flashnext:dev\",\n  \"torch\": \"2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\",\n  \"triton\": \"3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\",\n  \"fork_commit\": \"bdb6f0420e797de9266de593326368091085cc3b\",\n  \"image_digest\": \"sha256:175edc169402e327c4eed823caec30d196b7f824712e3a498333da87282f24de\",\n  \"wall_clock_s\": 839\n }\n}====\n# Marker: the instruments task lands fn_synctrace.py, fn_offload_batch.py and\n# fn_expert_union.py here; container/build.sh ensures this directory exists\n# so the Containerfile's COPY of the overlay is well-formed either way.\n====\n container/build.sh | 16 ++++++++++++----\n 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988041568},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The previous attempt's final commit (5ee2002) is complete, and it matches the built image (the receipt ts is 07:07:21Z = 09:07 local, which matches the image creation). The worktree was subsequently reset to a428fee (the branch HEAD), and the work has been lost from the branch — this is the failure mode that steering described.\n\nReconciliation: restore the branch to 5ee2002 (its parent is a428fee, exactly the current HEAD). Then verify that acceptance passes and the status is clean.\n\nBut wait — steering comment 4 says \"the last action MUST be: (1) run the acceptance argv yourself and confirm it passes; (2) git add only the paths within your conflict domain; (3) commit; (4) confirm that git status --porcelain is empty.\" If I just fast-forward to a dangling commit, I preserve the previous commit itself. This is the cleanest reconciliation, and it also satisfies \"commit the complete result.\" The commit's paths are all within the conflict domain (container/, results/receipts/).\n\nNext, run acceptance: bash -n container/build.sh && grep ... . Also, should I run the packaging tests too? The acceptance argv is what the judge will run, and I might also run the unittest suite to confirm the tree is sound (test_receipts_verify_runs_clean runs receipts-verify.py — build.json is pass, smoke.json is absent, weights receipt is present? results/receipts currently has weights-*.json — from a commit at the branch HEAD. Those existed in a428fee).\n\nLet me check the receipt at the branch HEAD: weights-coordinator.json and weights-worker.json exist. receipts-verify checks all receipts; the status must be pass. No problem.\n\nPlan:\n1. git reset --hard 5ee2002 (restore the previous attempt's commit to the branch).\n2. Run the acceptance argv.\n3. Optionally, also run the packaging tests (unittest discover tests/).\n4. Confirm that git status --porcelain is empty.\n\nConcern: is reset --hard okay? The current worktree is clean (status showed nothing? the earlier `git status --porcelain` output — the first line was empty, then the log). Yes, it's clean.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The last attempt completed a full execution (839-second build, pass receipt, and a verified image that's still present in podman storage), committed as `5ee2002`, but the branch was left sitting at its parent commit `a428fee` — so the work went missing from the lane. Reconciling means restoring that commit. Since its parent is precisely the current HEAD, we can fast-forward without any rewriting.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1ab69e76e9074bb0aaa9db0f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a871de4d3faa/container-recipe && git cat-file -p 5ee2002^{commit} | head -3 && git merge-base --is-ancestor a428fee 5ee2002 && echo \"a428fee is ancestor: clean fast-forward\" && git reset --hard 5ee2002 && git log --oneline -2 && git status --porcelain; echo \"porcelain-exit:$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":5768,"output":742,"cacheRead":23552,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":498,"totalTokens":30062,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988041572,"responseId":"chatcmpl-6c3b6aaa-3ec1-4742-96c8-a317485c1dbc","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1ab69e76e9074bb0aaa9db0f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"tree 222bed23fdb99e2f6f95d60410fb3d6289a877d9\nparent a428fee66b83d95682b418d5fdb4d975068e66ab\nauthor mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev> 1787987480 +0200\na428fee is ancestor: clean fast-forward\nHEAD is now at 5ee2002 container: recipe for flashnext:dev — pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\n5ee2002 container: recipe for flashnext:dev — pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\na428fee handoff: staging complete, campaign launches attended-by-daylight not overnight\nporcelain-exit:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988060120},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","